---
title: Clay Pot Chicken Rice Without the Clay Pot
servings: 4
course: dinner
cuisine: Chinese
tags: chicken, rice, quick, one-pan
source: https://www.food.com/recipe/76012
---

-- the source lists no amounts; these are sensible ones for four

Wash @long grain rice{400%g} under cold water, drain, then put it in the #rice cooker{} with @water{480%ml}, @garlic clove{2}(minced), @onion{1}(sliced), @oyster sauce{2%tbsp}, @dark soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @chicken thigh{400%g}(boneless skinless, cut into bite-size pieces), @chinese sausage{2}(sliced) and @white pepper{0.5%tsp}; stir everything together.

Cook the mixture in the #rice cooker{} as you normally would for rice, about ~{20%minutes}.

Garnish the cooked rice with @shallot{2}(thinly sliced) and @spring onion{2}(sliced).

If you like, drizzle a little more @&dark soy sauce{} over and serve.
